  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through next Monday)\nIssued at 1027 PM CDT Mon Aug 10 2026\n\nThe main H500 anti-cylonic system as seen by the latest global model \ndata shows a decent moisture transport advecting moisture from \nthe Gulf of America into the High Plains on the western periphery \nof mid level High pressure system. This should bring increased \nchances for showers and thunderstorms each afternoon and evening \nduring peak diurnal heating. Where the most favorable moisture \naxis sets up will be key to the highest POP chances overall. \nCurrently favoring the western Panhandles, but will watch and \nupdate forecast accordingly as we get closer to the end of the \nweek into the weekend for those rain chances. High temperatures \nwill remain above average for mid August.",
